# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` and fill in the real value.
#
#   Copy-Item .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# `.dev.vars` is gitignored and must never be committed. In production the key is set with:
#
#   npx wrangler secret put NEBIUS_API_KEY
#
# Note: `.dev.vars` is a wrangler file. `npm run dev` runs a plain Node Vite server with no
# Workers runtime, so it does NOT read this file — see src/lib/server-env.ts. Scripts and the
# dev server read the key from the environment instead; the probe script parses this file
# directly as a convenience.

NEBIUS_API_KEY=

# Optional: global spend ceiling for local runs. Production values live under `vars` in
# wrangler.jsonc. Set any of them to 0 to stop all model calls and see cached verdicts.
# GLOBAL_VERDICT_LIMIT=5000
# GLOBAL_TOKEN_LIMIT=5000000
# GLOBAL_USD_LIMIT=15

# Opens /exchanges, the log of every purchase the model contested. Pass it as ?key=<value>.
# Unset means the page stays closed, so the log is never published by forgetting something.
# It holds purchase labels and whatever people typed to explain themselves, which is why it
# is the one part of the app behind anything at all. In production:
#
#   npx wrangler secret put EXCHANGES_KEY
#
# EXCHANGES_KEY=

# Lets Bucket look something up before it reconsiders a contested purchase: whether the thing
# the person says broke can be repaired for less than a replacement costs. Credits come with
# the Nebius Builder Program. Without this key the second pass decides on their explanation
# and their history alone, which is how it worked before the lookup existed.
#
# Only the purchase label is ever sent, never what the person typed. See src/engine/evidence.ts.
#
#   npx wrangler secret put TAVILY_API_KEY
#
# TAVILY_API_KEY=

# PayPal entry (the `paypal` branch). Sandbox credentials for the Bucket sandbox app, from
# developer.paypal.com, Apps & Credentials, with the Sandbox toggle on. Turn on "Save payment
# methods" BEFORE the app issues its first token: PayPal reuses a token for hours and its
# permissions are fixed when it is issued. See docs/paypal-findings.md. In production:
#
#   npx wrangler secret put PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID
#   npx wrangler secret put PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET
#
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# The saved sandbox buyer wallet the demo pays from (a Vault payment token id). Lets judges try
# the flow without logging into PayPal.
# PAYPAL_DEMO_VAULT_ID=

# Sandbox unless this is exactly "live". Leave it unset for the hackathon.
# PAYPAL_ENV=

# How long a want waits in Sleep On It, in minutes. 1440 (24 hours) by default; set a few minutes
# for the demo so a hold can be watched expiring. Capped inside PayPal's 3-day honor period.
# HOLD_WINDOW_MINUTES=1440
